drm/v3d: merge the two v3d_cpu_job_free() destructors

Stable commit acd55ea40d03 ("drm/v3d: Fix use-after-free of CPU job query
arrays on error path") adds a v3d_cpu_job_free() kref destructor to
v3d_submit.c, which frees the timestamp and performance query arrays (and,
with c41ca6b0a0ac, the indirect CSD BO reference) and then calls
v3d_job_free().

rpi-6.12.y commit 2d693f4d08ff ("drm/v3d: CPU job submissions shouldn't
affect V3D GPU clock") already has a v3d_cpu_job_free() kref destructor,
which calls v3d_job_free_common(job, false) so that CPU jobs do not drop a
V3D clock reference they never took. Both merge without conflict, and the
build fails with:

  drivers/gpu/drm/v3d/v3d_submit.c:184:1: error: redefinition of 'v3d_cpu_job_free'

Keep the stable destructor and end it with
v3d_job_free_common(&job->base, false) instead of v3d_job_free(), so the
CPU job keeps skipping v3d_clock_up_put(), matching v3d_job_init() which
skips v3d_clock_up_get() for V3D_CPU.


diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/v3d/v3d_submit.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/v3d/v3d_submit.c
index 687a4a8ed90b..b772c21b7e34 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/v3d/v3d_submit.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/v3d/v3d_submit.c
@@ -158,14 +158,6 @@ v3d_job_free(struct kref *ref)
 	v3d_job_free_common(job, true);
 }
 
-static void
-v3d_cpu_job_free(struct kref *ref)
-{
-	struct v3d_job *job = container_of(ref, struct v3d_job, refcount);
-
-	v3d_job_free_common(job, false);
-}
-
 static void
 v3d_render_job_free(struct kref *ref)
 {
@@ -195,7 +187,7 @@ v3d_cpu_job_free(struct kref *ref)
 	if (job->indirect_csd.indirect)
 		drm_gem_object_put(job->indirect_csd.indirect);
 
-	v3d_job_free(ref);
+	v3d_job_free_common(&job->base, false);
 }
 
 void v3d_job_cleanup(struct v3d_job *job)
